[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Plains","oracle_id":"bc71ebf6-2056-41f7-be35-b2e5c34afa99","oracle_text":"({T}: Add {W}.)","power":null,"produced_mana":["W"],"released_at":"2026-11-13","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land — Plains"},{"cmc":8.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Morph"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{7}{U}","name":"Scornful Egotist","oracle_id":"455cbf35-f340-4f1f-a331-5b082c9034ec","oracle_text":"Morph {U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)","power":"1","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2003-05-26","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature — Human Wizard"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":["B"],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Swamp","oracle_id":"56719f6a-1a6c-4c0a-8d21-18f7d7350b68","oracle_text":"({T}: Add {B}.)","power":null,"produced_mana":["B"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land — Swamp"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"A face-down creature has no name, so it can't share a name with anything. This includes other creatures with no name.","oracle_id":"4f9e07ae-6341-4b46-9f77-f17ab659d266","published_at":"2019-01-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the entering creature is put into your graveyard while Guardian Project's ability is on the stack, that same card will be a creature card in your graveyard that shares a name with the creature that was on the battlefield, so you won't draw a card.","oracle_id":"4f9e07ae-6341-4b46-9f77-f17ab659d266","published_at":"2019-01-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the entering creature leaves the battlefield and returns while Guardian Project's ability is on the stack, that same card will be a new creature you control that shares a name with the creature that was on the battlefield, so you won't draw a card. However, Guardian Project's ability may trigger for the new creature and you may draw a card as that ability resolves.","oracle_id":"4f9e07ae-6341-4b46-9f77-f17ab659d266","published_at":"2019-01-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Whether the entering creature shares a name with a creature you control or a creature card in your graveyard is checked both as that creature enters and as Guardian Project's ability resolves. If the entering creature isn't the first of its name as it enters, the ability doesn't trigger at all; if its name is shared as the ability resolves, you don't draw a card.","oracle_id":"4f9e07ae-6341-4b46-9f77-f17ab659d266","published_at":"2019-01-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
